0007: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0008:     """
0009:     Use the left-edge color legend to draw a padded rectangular halo around each matching object while preserving enclosed holes.
0010: 
0011:     Input structure:
0012:     - The grid has a dominant background color.
0013:     - One or more two-row markers sit on the left edge; each marker is a 2x2 block whose left column is an object color and right column is its halo color.
0014:     - Away from the markers, every source color from the legend appears as one or more 4-connected monochrome objects.
0015: 
0016:     Rule:
0017:     - Keep the input pixels unchanged.
0018:     - For each source-color object, take its tight bbox expanded by one cell and clipped to the grid.
0019:     - Recolor background pixels in that expanded region to the marker's halo color, except for background holes enclosed by the object.
0020: 
0021:     Key insight:
0022:     - The small left-edge bars are a legend: they map object colors to the colors used for the surrounding padded bbox.
0023:     """
