0046:     - Optional non-background control pixels may sit in the channel between the two paths.
0047: 
0048:     Rule
0049:     - Dilate each path component by one cell in the 8-neighborhood and intersect the two dilations; this gives the one-cell-wide middle channel.
0050:     - A control pixel in that channel is a blocker only when its 4-neighbors touch fewer than both path components; otherwise it is part of the channel and is repainted.
0051:     - After removing blockers, paint the channel component connected to the top edge teal and keep all other pixels unchanged.
